# Citation metadata for this repository and the technical report it accompanies.
# license: MIT covers this repository's own code and docs only; README.md, "License
# and third-party material", lists what it does not cover (measurement-db, the
# organisers' code, formative tables and inventory rows).
# version: the release tag (docs/release.md, section 6), not the Python package's
# version in pyproject.toml.
# keywords: the same list as the "Keywords:" line of docs/report/draft.md, which fills
# the PDF's metadata (tests/test_build_report_pdf.py checks they agree).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the technical report below."
type: software
title: "Calibrating a hierarchical response model for a benchmark-level cold start"
abstract: >-
  Code, results and report source for an entry to the Predictive AI Evaluation
  Competition (PAIEC) at NeurIPS 2026: a replica of the organisers' streaming
  evaluator, a hierarchical item-response predictor fitted from the revealed
  labels alone, the calibration of its prior on a new benchmark's level on
  test-like runs built from public data, and one script per reported number.
authors:
